issues.body:
Every Armature feature in Stator (issue chips, the issue, issue list, chart and roadmap blocks, the calendar's due issues, creating issues from selected text, the remote links back to pages, the webhook and following the Armature theme) is tested only against `armature-stub`. The stub is held to a copy of Armature's `api/openapi.json` pinned at `b974701`, from before Armature's changes of 2026-10-14 (`/api/v1/meta`, capabilities, the webhook envelope version, the `dynamo` realm). Nothing shows that Stator works with a real Armature.

- Refresh the vendored contract (`make armature-openapi REF=<current main>`), record the ref in `api/armature/SOURCE`, and fix whatever the stub or the client no longer matches.
- A test layer that runs Stator against a real Armature, built from a pinned ref of Cloudster1/Armature (its own compose stack or images built from it), seeded with a project, issues with dates, an epic and a team, and a member with a personal access token:
  - connecting Armature in the settings and storing a token;
  - each slash block (Armature issue, Armature issue list, Armature chart, Armature roadmap) and a chip show real issues as that member may see them, and a second member without access sees "Not available";
  - creating issues from selected text files them in Armature;
  - publishing a page puts the remote link on the issue in Armature, and trashing the page takes it away;
  - a change in Armature reaches the page through the signed webhook;
  - following the Armature theme.
- It runs in CI (its own job, allowed to take longer) and locally through a Makefile target; the pinned Armature ref is in one place so Dynamo can reuse it.
- Where the real Armature and the stub disagree, the stub follows Armature.

